            ","id":587},{"type":2,"tagName":"div","attributes":{"class":"row highlight-row"},"childNodes":[{"type":3,"textContent":"
                ","id":589},{"type":2,"tagName":"div","attributes":{"class":"col-md-4 col-sm-6"},"childNodes":[{"type":3,"textContent":"
                    ","id":591},{"type":2,"tagName":"div","attributes":{"class":"highlight-card"},"childNodes":[{"type":3,"textContent":"
                        ","id":593},{"type":2,"tagName":"i","attributes":{"class":"fa fa-shield highlight-icon","aria-hidden":"true"},"childNodes":[],"id":594},{"type":3,"textContent":"
                        ","id":595},{"type":2,"tagName":"h3","attributes":{},"childNodes":[{"type":3,"textContent":"Cleared a Three-Month Safety Backlog","id":597}],"id":596},{"type":3,"textContent":"
                        ","id":598},{"type":2,"tagName":"p","attributes":{},"childNodes":[{"type":3,"textContent":"An AI assistant's flagged responses needed human review under strict data privacy rules, and the queue was up to a three-month backlog. Digging
                            into the reporting data, I found that almost half of everything flagged traced back to a
                            single false-positive pattern. Retiring that one rule cut the volume dramatically, and I
                            built the triage process and documentation so any on-call engineer could keep the queue
                            current weekly.","id":600}],"id":599},{"type":3,"textContent":"
                    ","id":601}],"id":592},{"type":3,"textContent":"
                ","id":602}],"id":590},{"type":3,"textContent":"

                ","id":603},{"type":2,"tagName":"div","attributes":{"class":"col-md-4 col-sm-6"},"childNodes":[{"type":3,"textContent":"
                    ","id":605},{"type":2,"tagName":"div","attributes":{"class":"highlight-card"},"childNodes":[{"type":3,"textContent":"
                        ","id":607},{"type":2,"tagName":"i","attributes":{"class":"fa fa-balance-scale highlight-icon","aria-hidden":"true"},"childNodes":[],"id":608},{"type":3,"textContent":"
                        ","id":609},{"type":2,"tagName":"h3","attributes":{},"childNodes":[{"type":3,"textContent":"Turned a Build-vs-Buy Question Into a One-Sprint Win","id":611}],"id":610},{"type":3,"textContent":"
                        ","id":612},{"type":2,"tagName":"p","attributes":{},"childNodes":[{"type":3,"textContent":"Product wanted a fully custom emoji picker; the design was beautiful and the estimate was
                            heavy. Rather than push back or just build it, I researched the real options and brought stakeholders a clear side-by-side of speed versus customization. We
                            shipped a well-chosen off-the-shelf solution inside a single sprint. Users loved it
                            immediately, and the custom styling nobody missed stayed safely in the backlog.","id":614}],"id":613},{"type":3,"textContent":"
                    ","id":615}],"id":606},{"type":3,"textContent":"
                ","id":616}],"id":604},{"type":3,"textContent":"

                ","id":617},{"type":2,"tagName":"div","attributes":{"class":"col-md-4 col-sm-6"},"childNodes":[{"type":3,"textContent":"
                    ","id":619},{"type":2,"tagName":"div","attributes":{"class":"highlight-card"},"childNodes":[{"type":3,"textContent":"
                        ","id":621},{"type":2,"tagName":"i","attributes":{"class":"fa fa-sitemap highlight-icon","aria-hidden":"true"},"childNodes":[],"id":622},{"type":3,"textContent":"
                        ","id":623},{"type":2,"tagName":"h3","attributes":{},"childNodes":[{"type":3,"textContent":"Led a Feature Through Every Edge Case","id":625}],"id":624},{"type":3,"textContent":"
                        ","id":626},{"type":2,"tagName":"p","attributes":{},"childNodes":[{"type":3,"textContent":"I led an extension to a collaborative feature that changed use based on permissions. The behavior looked simple until you asked the real questions —
                            what happens with two admin users, or when a new admin is added? Is an admin able to alter any users content? I built a
                            decision matrix, worked through each case with product, and shipped with every scenario
                            defined. I also wrote the documentation the original feature had never had, which outlived
                            my part of the project.","id":628}],"id":627},{"type":3,"textContent":"
                    ","id":629}],"id":620},{"type":3,"textContent":"
                ","id":630}],"id":618},{"type":3,"textContent":"

                ","id":631},{"type":2,"tagName":"div","attributes":{"class":"col-md-4 col-sm-6"},"childNodes":[{"type":3,"textContent":"
                    ","id":633},{"type":2,"tagName":"div","attributes":{"class":"highlight-card"},"childNodes":[{"type":3,"textContent":"
                        ","id":635},{"type":2,"tagName":"i","attributes":{"class":"fa fa-paint-brush highlight-icon","aria-hidden":"true"},"childNodes":[],"id":636},{"type":3,"textContent":"
                        ","id":637},{"type":2,"tagName":"h3","attributes":{},"childNodes":[{"type":3,"textContent":"Replaced a Legacy UI Layer Ahead of Schedule","id":639}],"id":638},{"type":3,"textContent":"
                        ","id":640},{"type":2,"tagName":"p","attributes":{},"childNodes":[{"type":3,"textContent":"I joined a startup as the senior front-end engineer to strip out an aging component framework
                            and replace it with custom UI. As the only front-end-focused developer, I had real autonomy
                            over the approach, and I chose reusable, composable components that could later be lifted
                            into a proper library. The team had budgeted far longer; I finished in under six months, and
                            handed the foundation to the next front-end hire before I left.","id":642}],"id":641},{"type":3,"textContent":"
                    ","id":643}],"id":634},{"type":3,"textContent":"
                ","id":644}],"id":632},{"type":3,"textContent":"

                ","id":645},{"type":2,"tagName":"div","attributes":{"class":"col-md-4 col-sm-6"},"childNodes":[{"type":3,"textContent":"
                    ","id":647},{"type":2,"tagName":"div","attributes":{"class":"highlight-card"},"childNodes":[{"type":3,"textContent":"
                        ","id":649},{"type":2,"tagName":"i","attributes":{"class":"fa fa-refresh highlight-icon","aria-hidden":"true"},"childNodes":[],"id":650},{"type":3,"textContent":"
                        ","id":651},{"type":2,"tagName":"h3","attributes":{},"childNodes":[{"type":3,"textContent":"Rewrote a High-Traffic Site in React","id":653}],"id":652},{"type":3,"textContent":"
                        ","id":654},{"type":2,"tagName":"p","attributes":{},"childNodes":[{"type":3,"textContent":"I was a major contributor on the rewrite of a heavily trafficked site from an early
                            JavaScript framework into React, my first real experience with a shared component library
                            and design system. Two of my three teammates were new to React and one was new to JavaScript
                            entirely, so a lot of the work was translating technical decisions for mixed audiences and
                            teaching as we went. It turned into two-way mentoring — I learned as much about
                            large-scale architecture as they learned about React.","id":656}],"id":655},{"type":3,"textContent":"
                    ","id":657}],"id":648},{"type":3,"textContent":"
                ","id":658}],"id":646},{"type":3,"textContent":"

                ","id":659},{"type":2,"tagName":"div","attributes":{"class":"col-md-4 col-sm-6"},"childNodes":[{"type":3,"textContent":"
                    ","id":661},{"type":2,"tagName":"div","attributes":{"class":"highlight-card"},"childNodes":[{"type":3,"textContent":"
                        ","id":663},{"type":2,"tagName":"i","attributes":{"class":"fa fa-cubes highlight-icon","aria-hidden":"true"},"childNodes":[],"id":664},{"type":3,"textContent":"
                        ","id":665},{"type":2,"tagName":"h3","attributes":{},"childNodes":[{"type":3,"textContent":"Shipped a Design System Against a Public Deadline","id":667}],"id":666},{"type":3,"textContent":"
                        ","id":668},{"type":2,"tagName":"p","attributes":{},"childNodes":[{"type":3,"textContent":"A brand-new internal design system landed on my team with a launch date already announced
                            publicly. The components didn't match how our app actually passed state, so we designed an
                            adapter layer of wrapper components to get the new system into production on time —
                            then went back and methodically retired that layer over the following months. We hit the
                            date, the product looked great, and the team stayed intact and working well together
                            through a genuinely frustrating stretch.","id":670}],"id":669},{"type":3,"textContent":"
                    ","id":671}],"id":662},{"type":3,"textContent":"
                ","id":672}],"id":660},{"type":3,"textContent":"

                ","id":673},{"type":2,"tagName":"div","attributes":{"class":"col-md-4 col-sm-6"},"childNodes":[{"type":3,"textContent":"
                    ","id":675},{"type":2,"tagName":"div","attributes":{"class":"highlight-card"},"childNodes":[{"type":3,"textContent":"
                        ","id":677},{"type":2,"tagName":"i","attributes":{"class":"fa fa-television highlight-icon","aria-hidden":"true"},"childNodes":[],"id":678},{"type":3,"textContent":"
                        ","id":679},{"type":2,"tagName":"h3","attributes":{},"childNodes":[{"type":3,"textContent":"Learned a Niche Language to Ship on TV","id":681}],"id":680},{"type":3,"textContent":"
                        ","id":682},{"type":2,"tagName":"p","attributes":{},"childNodes":[{"type":3,"textContent":"Moving onto a streaming-TV team meant picking up BrightScript, a language used almost
                            nowhere else, and learning the constraints of set-top boxes and smart TVs. I got productive
                            quickly by leaning on what carries across languages rather than starting from zero, and
                            shipped features to devices for millions of users. It's a great reminder that the fundamentals transfer further than the syntax does.","id":684}],"id":683},{"type":3,"textContent":"
                    ","id":685}],"id":676},{"type":3,"textContent":"
                ","id":686}],"id":674},{"type":3,"textContent":"

                ","id":687},{"type":2,"tagName":"div","attributes":{"class":"col-md-4 col-sm-6"},"childNodes":[{"type":3,"textContent":"
                    ","id":689},{"type":2,"tagName":"div","attributes":{"class":"highlight-card"},"childNodes":[{"type":3,"textContent":"
                        ","id":691},{"type":2,"tagName":"i","attributes":{"class":"fa fa-flask highlight-icon","aria-hidden":"true"},"childNodes":[],"id":692},{"type":3,"textContent":"
                        ","id":693},{"type":2,"tagName":"h3","attributes":{},"childNodes":[{"type":3,"textContent":"Became the Go-To for Experimentation","id":695}],"id":694},{"type":3,"textContent":"
                        ","id":696},{"type":2,"tagName":"p","attributes":{},"childNodes":[{"type":3,"textContent":"On a mature, high-traffic product I became the subject-matter expert on our A/B testing
                            platform, working closely with the analytics team to make sure experiments produced data
                            people could actually act on. For one test I built out an independent backend and API just
                            to organize the results properly. I also took 24/7 monitoring shifts during a major
                            national election, watching dashboards through the highest-traffic nights of the year.","id":698}],"id":697},{"type":3,"textContent":"
                    ","id":699}],"id":690},{"type":3,"textContent":"
                ","id":700}],"id":688},{"type":3,"textContent":"

                ","id":701},{"type":2,"tagName":"div","attributes":{"class":"col-md-4 col-sm-6"},"childNodes":[{"type":3,"textContent":"
                    ","id":703},{"type":2,"tagName":"div","attributes":{"class":"highlight-card"},"childNodes":[{"type":3,"textContent":"
                        ","id":705},{"type":2,"tagName":"i","attributes":{"class":"fa fa-mobile highlight-icon","aria-hidden":"true"},"childNodes":[],"id":706},{"type":3,"textContent":"
                        ","id":707},{"type":2,"tagName":"h3","attributes":{},"childNodes":[{"type":3,"textContent":"Built a Mobile App From Scratch","id":709}],"id":708},{"type":3,"textContent":"
                        ","id":710},{"type":2,"tagName":"p","attributes":{},"childNodes":[{"type":3,"textContent":"At a company of under twenty people, I built a React Native app from an empty repository
                            with one other engineer, owning the UI side end to end for a complex product that paying
                            customers depended on. The piece I'm proudest of is a drag-and-drop scheduling interface:
                            no existing package did what we needed, so I took an open-source foundation apart and
                            rebuilt it to our requirements. It taught me more about ownership than any project since.","id":712}],"id":711},{"type":3,"textContent":"
